.TH PKG-INSTALL-AUR 1 "2026-08-07" "pkg-install-aur" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pkg-install-aur \- interactive AUR package installer (fzf TUI)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pkg-install-aur
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pkg-install-aur
is an interactive
.BR fzf (1)
front end for installing packages from the Arch User Repository (AUR).
It takes no command\-line arguments; the whole workflow happens inside the
fzf list and its preview pane.
.P
On start, the script lists every AUR package (\fByay \-Slqa\fR, bare
package names) and feeds it to
.BR fzf (1).
Unlike
.BR pkg-install (1),
no installed state marker is added, because the AUR source list contains
names only. Filter by typing, toggle entries into the selection with
.B Tab
and press Enter. The chosen package names are collected and installed in
a single call to
.BR paru (1)
(\fBparu \-S \-\-noconfirm\fR), which builds the AUR packages and their
dependencies, so no further confirmation is asked. If the selection is
empty (the list is dismissed), the script exits silently without making
any change.
.P
A wrap\-enabled preview pane at the bottom (65% of the screen) shows
detailed information for the highlighted package via
.BR yay (1)
(\fByay \-Siia\fR, using field \fB{1}\fR, the package name). The pointer
and multi\-select marker are shown in green, and the preview label reads:
.IP
\fBalt\-p: toggle preview | alt\-j/k: scroll preview | tab: multi\-select\fR
.SS Key bindings
.IP \(bu 2
.B Tab
toggle multi\-selection of the current entry
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-J
move the cursor down the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Ctrl-K
move the cursor up the list
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-P
toggle the preview pane
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-D
scroll the preview half a page down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-U
scroll the preview half a page up
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-J
scroll the preview one line down
.IP \(bu 2
.B Alt-K
scroll the preview one line up
.P
The script requires
.BR fzf (1),
.BR yay (1)
and
.BR paru (1).
.SH EXAMPLES
Install one or more AUR packages:
.IP
.EX
pkg-install-aur
.EE
.P
Type a search term to filter, press
.B Tab
on each package of interest, then press Enter to build and install all of
them.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR paru (1),
.BR yay (1),
.BR fzf (1),
.BR pkg-install (1),
.BR pkg-remove.sh (1)
